  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1123 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nSurface high pressure will linger into the start of the weekend, \nsupporting a warming trend behind the departing system. Highs \non Friday are forecast to rebound into the mid-40s before climbing\nfurther on Saturday as the region enters the warm sector of a \nlow-pressure system tracking across central Canada, promoting \nsouthwesterly warm-air advection. However, beginning Sunday, the\nassociated cold front will sweep through the region, bringing \nincreased chances for rain showers to close out the weekend. \nSurface high pressure will return for Monday, ushering in dry \nconditions and near-seasonal temperatures through the remainder \nof the forecast period.",
